[
  {
    "id": "sitl42-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 42 Terrain goto",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "Move's goto with altRef=terrain against ArduCopter sysid 1: the third altitude reference packs MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_TERRAIN_ALT (10) on the DO_REPOSITION carrier and nothing else — the vehicle resolves height-above-terrain from its own terrain data (pymavlink posture, owner ruling 2026-08-23). Both honest outcomes PASS: ACCEPTED when the SITL has terrain data, DENIED/FAILED when it has none — the frame rode the wire and the answer came back loud. Only silence fails.",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl42-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl42-tab",
    "name": "Move goto, altRef=terrain — frame 10 rides the wire",
    "info": "Flow: Arm (COMMAND_LONG) -> Takeoff 10 m (COMMAND_LONG) -> delay -> Move goto, Send & confirm (COMMAND_INT / DO_REPOSITION, altitude above terrain = GLOBAL_TERRAIN_ALT 10, 15 m, modest offset from home).\n\nPrerequisite: ArduCopter in GUIDED before the chain fires (harness prep ap-guided-1). CHANGE_MODE off, same as SITL 27 — the frame is the only variable against that run.\n\nWhat this run measures (§14): the terrain frame reaches the vehicle and the vehicle's own answer surfaces on output 1. The lab's terrain-data state is unmeasured, so ACCEPTED (terrain data present) and a loud refusal (none) are BOTH correct driver behavior under the ruling — we serve no tiles and check nothing."
  },
